# Provenance for the vendored Ghostty web terminal artifact.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE RE-VENDORING. The artifact is NOT upstream 0.4.8 verbatim —
# it is a local fork. `git log --follow -- assets/vendor/ghostty.js` shows 15
# commits on top of the original vendor drop, several of which fix bugs that
# cost real debugging time:
#
#   433c91ae  fit on container rect, not pre rect
#   b920a0ed  lock advance width so cursor lines up with chars
#   c3da04d3  pin pre line-height so cursor row math matches layout
#   61d6adab  pin pre line-height as integer px to kill cursor-row drift
#   71fdb580  pre fills container via absolute inset
#   030c0652  map clicks through display scale
#   62bd189e  coalesce identical-style cell runs in renderCells
#   90d9faf5  let browser dev shortcuts through in raw terminal mode
#
# Re-fetching `upstream_revision` and overwriting the artifact WILL SILENTLY
# DROP all of them, reintroducing cursor-row drift, wrong advance width, and
# scale-broken clicks. To take an upstream update, re-apply these commits on top
# of the new drop and then refresh `artifact_sha256` — do not just replace the
# file.
#
# `upstream_*` and `hex_*` below describe the ANCESTOR the fork started from.
# `artifact_sha256` describes the FORKED file that Casein actually ships, and is
# what scripts/check-vendor-pin-guard.sh compares against.

